DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ppkkgg__mmkkllooccaatteeddbb command is used to create a file database for binary
     packages, which can be searched using the locate(1) utility.

     Entries created for each package will have the package name prepended:
     kdelibs-3.3.2p2:/usr/local/bin/meinproc.

     If the --pp option is used, and SUBDIRLIST is not defined, ppkkgg__mmkkllooccaatteeddbb
     will retrieve all package entries from the ports tree.

     If the --pp option is used together with SUBDIRLIST, ppkkgg__mmkkllooccaatteeddbb will
     retrieve the package entries listed in SUBDIRLIST from the ports tree.

     Otherwise, ppkkgg__mmkkllooccaatteeddbb will build database entries for every file ob‐
     ject for each _p_k_g_-_n_a_m_e given on the command line, or for every package in
     a _r_e_p_o_s_i_t_o_r_y specified as the --dd option.  If no package name is given,
     ppkkgg__mmkkllooccaatteeddbb will build database entries for all currently installed
     packages.

     By default (unless standard output is a terminal), the list of names is
     fed to _/_u_s_r_/_l_i_b_e_x_e_c_/_l_o_c_a_t_e_._m_k_l_o_c_a_t_e_d_b and the end result should be redi‐
     rected to a file.

     The options are as follows:

     --aa      Prepend file names with pkgpath information and package names.

     --dd _r_e_p_o_s_i_t_o_r_y
             Scan directory _r_e_p_o_s_i_t_o_r_y for packages.

     --KK      Include keyword in each object full name.  This is more accurate,
             but defeats locate(1) compression.

             However, note that some meta annotations always make it into the
             database: @@**eexxeecc**, @@ddeeffiinnee--ttaagg, @@nneewwggrroouupp, @@nneewwuusseerr, @@ooppttiioonn
             _n_o_-_d_e_f_a_u_l_t_-_c_o_n_f_l_i_c_t and @@ttaagg.

     --nn      Do not pipe output to _/_u_s_r_/_l_i_b_e_x_e_c_/_l_o_c_a_t_e_._m_k_l_o_c_a_t_e_d_b (default if
             standard output is a terminal).

     --PP      Prepend file names with pkgpath information instead of package
             name.

     --pp _p_o_r_t_s_d_i_r
             Retrieve packing-lists from the ports tree instead of binary
             packages.

     --qq      Be quiet: do not report every package processed to standard er‐
             ror.

     --uu      Update an existing list.  The list must come from standard input,
             and contain pkgpath information for items to be replaced.

